Kernel_executeFromExecutor
├── when the caller is not an installed executor
│   └── it should revert with Unauthorized error
└── when the caller is an installed executor
    ├── given the execution mode execType is unsupported
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidExecType error
    ├── given the executor has a hook configured
    │   ├── it should call preHook on the executor hook before execution
    │   ├── given preHook reverts
    │   │   └── it should propagate the revert
    │   └── given preHook succeeds
    │       ├── it should execute the requested operations
    │       ├── it should call postHook on the executor hook after execution
    │       ├── given postHook reverts
    │       │   └── it should propagate the revert
    │       └── given postHook succeeds
    │           └── it should return the execution results
    ├── given the executor has hook set to address1
    │   ├── it should skip preHook and postHook calls
    │   └── it should execute the requested operations directly
    ├── given the execution mode callType is SINGLE
    │   ├── given the execution mode execType is DEFAULT
    │   │   ├── when the target call succeeds
    │   │   │   └── it should return the result in returnData array
    │   │   └── when the target call reverts
    │   │       └── it should propagate the revert
    │   └── given the execution mode execType is TRY
    │       ├── when the target call succeeds
    │       │   └── it should return the result in returnData array
    │       └── when the target call reverts
    │           ├── it should NOT propagate the revert
    │           └── it should return empty bytes for the failed call
    ├── given the execution mode callType is BATCH
    │   ├── given the execution mode execType is DEFAULT
    │   │   ├── when all calls succeed
    │   │   │   └── it should return all results in returnData array
    │   │   └── when any call reverts
    │   │       └── it should propagate the revert
    │   └── given the execution mode execType is TRY
    │       ├── when all calls succeed
    │       │   └── it should return all results in returnData array
    │       └── when any call reverts
    │           ├── it should NOT propagate the revert
    │           ├── it should return empty bytes for the failed call
    │           └── it should continue executing remaining calls
    ├── given the execution mode callType is DELEGATECALL
        ├── given the execution mode execType is DEFAULT
        │   ├── when the delegatecall succeeds
        │   │   └── it should return the result
        │   └── when the delegatecall reverts
        │       └── it should propagate the revert
        └── given the execution mode execType is TRY
            ├── when the delegatecall succeeds
            │   └── it should return the result
            └── when the delegatecall reverts
                ├── it should NOT propagate the revert
                └── it should return empty bytes
    └── given the execution mode callType is unsupported
        └── it should revert with InvalidCallType error
